      "id": "n493-module",
      "name": "N493 rotary thermal-management module",
      "system": "cooling-hvac",
      "assembly": "engine-cooling",
      "subAssembly": null,
      "oemPartNumber": "06L121111P",
      "description": "R9 RESOLUTION: the leak-prone plastic pump/thermostat unit IS the N493 module, standard on all EA888 Gen 3 (SSP 606 + erWin Rep. Gr. 19). Map-controlled coolant 85–107 °C with the wax safety thermostat only as a 113 °C fallback. Supersession 06L121111 → 06L121111P; module bolts 9 Nm. The Audi/Schaeffler rotary-slide valve module replacing a wax thermostat: valve 1 regulates oil-cooler/head/radiator flow (~80–110 °C, up to ~107 °C light-load for low friction), valve 2 couples the block in at ~145° of valve-1 rotation. Driven by one DC motor through a worm gear; 12 V / 1,000 Hz PWM control (dossier §2).",
      "material": null,
      "torqueSpec": null,
      "knownIssues": [
        "THE classic Gen 3 coolant weak point: the plastic housing near the hot side goes brittle and cracks/leaks, typically 60,000–90,000 miles. Aftermarket reinforced/metal housings exist (dossier §2)."
